   $q$Listen. Goat looked into the pond and saw a goat in the water staring back. Goat thought the other goat looked angry. Goat lowered its horns and charged right at it. Splash! Goat landed in the cold water and saw that the other goat had only been Goat's own face. From then on, Goat took a good look before rushing in. What is the lesson of this story? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Keep your word","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Keep your word"}},{"text":"Think before you act","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Think before you act"}},{"text":"Work as a team","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Work as a team"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Think before you act$q$, $q$Goat charged without stopping to think and fell in the pond. The angry goat was only Goat's own face. The lesson is think before you act.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
