   $q$Listen. In a village by the hills, an old woman in a torn coat knocked on doors, asking for water. The first family shut the door. The second family said they were too busy. A boy named Tenzin gave her a cup of cool water and a piece of bread. The old woman smiled and gave Tenzin a seed that grew into a tree full of sweet fruit. What is the lesson of this story? Tap the answer.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Keep trying","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Keep trying"}},{"text":"Plan ahead","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Plan ahead"}},{"text":"Be kind to all","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Be kind to all"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Be kind to all$q$, $q$Tenzin was kind to the old woman when others were not, and the kindness brought a fruit tree. The lesson is be kind to all.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
