   $q$Which sentence from the passage tells a cause and its effect?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Because their wings work like paddles, penguins are faster swimmers than puffins.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Most penguins live in the southern half of the world.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-cause"},{"text":"\"They flap their small wings very fast and zoom over the waves.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-cause"},{"text":"\"A puffin has a bright orange and yellow beak in spring.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-cause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Because their wings work like paddles, penguins are faster swimmers than puffins."$q$, $q$This sentence uses "Because" to show that paddle-like wings cause penguins to swim faster. The sentence about the puffin's beak only describes how it looks; it does not tell why something happens.$q$, 'draft', '93f7e269-392d-5072-bd4b-5deb3fc38102')
